    "body": "fix on issue/1521-plasma-cut-data · PR #2681 · pinned by plasma_recipe_thicker_than_the_pierce_capacity_needs_an_edge_start, plasma_recipe_is_picked_by_material_and_exact_thickness_only, plasma_recipe_commands_refuse_bad_rows_by_tool_name_and_undo_restores, plasma_recipes_roundtrip_project_and_library_and_never_seed_by_material_alone, a_torch_recipe_rides_the_draft_and_is_not_drawn_as_a_material_row (12 new pins; all named in the PR) · merges at the next cut\n\nThe PR is slice 1 only, the tool side: the plasma recipe record on the torch cutting rows, its refusals and the file round trip.\nThe PR says `Refs #1521`. It does not close this issue.\nThe PR is a `feat`, because it adds a capability.\n\nThis work stays open here:\n\n- The operation picks a row and overrides single values (the rest of slice 1).\n- Plasma generation and the Tormach post use the row; the edge-start rule is verified (slice 2). That slice must take the project file version step.\n- Gas type and gas pressure on the recipe.\n- An editor for the recipes on the tool page.\n- Laser and waterjet pierce stages, docs and example rows (slices 3 to 5).\n\nThe decision record is `docs/decisions/1521-plasma-cut-data.md` on the branch.\n",
